`loop\`, a human gate on \`awaitSignal\`, an \`action\` naming a handler, plus \`map\`, \`gate\`, \`childWorkflow\`, \`sleep\`, \`onTrigger\` and \`escalation\`. The \`@corbits/*\` packages on npm: \`@corbits/artifacts\` for versioned files, \`@corbits/react-ui\` for the components a generated interface draws from, \`@corbits/oauth-core\` for an OAuth flow, the provider and adapter packages for model connectors; the \`@intx/tools-*\` packages are an agent step's tools. The corbits-packages skill is the full list with versions.\\n\\n## The artifact\\n\\nYour document is the artifact of the kind your \\"Stage document\\" section names,\\nshown beside the conversation, so the reply carries no part of it and no\\nheading. End the reply with your one question and its \`- Option:\` lines;\\nwith nothing to ask, end it after what changed, with no line saying so.\\n\\nThe first time, call artifact_write with no artifactId, the stage kind, a short\\ntitle and the full content. After that, revise the same artifact: its\\nartifactId, expectedVersion set to the version you last wrote, and edits that\\nreplace the passages that change, so each point stays once; send whole content\\nonly when most of it changes.\\nKeep one artifact per document. If a write is refused, read the artifact once\\nwith artifact_read and try again.\\n\\n## Stage document\\n\\nYou are the Build and test specialist. Your document is recorded under the kind \`build_evidence\`; pass that kind to artifact_write when you create it.",
  tools: [artifacts],
  capabilities: [],
  inference: { sources: [SOURCE] },
});

export default defineWorkflow({
  id: "sb-stage-8",
  triggers: [{ type: "mail", to: "sb-stage-8@solutions-builder.local" }],
  credentialBindings: [
    {
      package: "@corbits/artifacts/sidecar-bundle",
      handle: "hub",
      provider: "sb-workflow-artifacts",
      name: "workflow-artifacts:build-supervisor",
      locator: "tenant",
    },
  ],
  grantRequirements: [
    {
      resource: "credential:*",
      action: "use",
      source: "creator",
      conditions: { tool: "tool:@corbits/artifacts/sidecar-bundle" },
    },
  ],
  steps: {
    run: step({
      agent: AGENT,
      input: { from: "trigger.payload" },
      drainBehavior: "wait",
